diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5d0a5ff
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+The coffee-art canvas is rendered by C compiled to WebAssembly. A dedicated
+module worker loads Emscripten and computes every pixel; the page only copies
+the finished RGBA buffer to a canvas. Initial rendering is automatic, and the
+button requests a fresh seed. Status announcements, failure recovery, and a
+timeout keep the interaction usable.
+
+## Build and run
+
+Requires Node.js 22+ and Emscripten (`emcc` on PATH; verified with 6.0.1).
+
+```sh
+npm install
+npm run build
+npm run preview
+```
+
+Deploy the complete `dist` directory, including its generated worker and Wasm
+assets. `npm start` starts development mode. No cross-origin isolation headers
+or SharedArrayBuffer are needed.
+
+The build uses `-Oz -flto -g0`, ES modules, strict mode, memory growth, and no
+dynamic linking. The browser environment includes `worker` because execution
+occurs in a dedicated worker, alongside `web`; Node and shell are excluded.
+
+## Verification
+
+```sh
+npm run build:assertions
+npx playwright test
+npm run build
+npx playwright test
+```
+
+Tests exercise actual Wasm loading, initial and repeated rendering, main-thread
+responsiveness under CPU throttling, clean browser console output, and recovery
+from a failed Wasm fetch. Set `CHROME_PATH` to your Chrome executable when it is
+not located at `/opt/google/chrome/chrome`.
